  "description": "Establish the normalized CPU LDPC throughput gap against AFF3CT and rank measured bottlenecks before decoder optimization.\n\n## Background\n\nThe existing comparison harness in dev/benchmarks/gf2-sim/comparison exports identical parity-check matrices for DVB-T2 rate-1/2 normal frames and the NR BG1 Z=384 mother code. Earlier throughput columns did not normalize worker counts or affinity and therefore do not establish the per-core competitive gap. This issue owns profiling and recommendations, not decoder optimization implementation.\n\n## Success Criteria\n\n- [hard] REQ-01: Publish pinned-thread, quiet-host comparisons for both existing configurations: one worker versus one worker, and 24 versus 24 logical-CPU workers, augmented with six- and twelve-physical-core arms. Resolve topology and record affinity, actual worker counts, nested thread pools, SMT state and source/build identities.\n\n- [hard] REQ-02: Identify at least three leading hot-path contributors with measured time shares and committed perf profiles or equivalent evidence, including allocation, edge traversal, layout, reduction and dispatch costs where present. Distinguish single-core bottlenecks from multicore saturation.\n\n- [hard] REQ-03: Rank candidate levers using measured evidence or labeled estimates: allocation removal, canonical edge indexing, flat check/variable-major message layouts, shared min/second-min/sign reductions, inter-frame SIMD, quantized/layered decoding and QC-aware intra-frame work. Include batch conversion, syndrome/termination and degree-structure costs; name a falsifiable workload experiment for each recommendation.\n\n- [hard] REQ-04: Preserve the existing numerical comparison contract: identical H, NMS alpha 0.75, flooding schedule, iteration cap 50 and syndrome early termination in matched arms; feed identical recorded LLRs where the adapter supports it. Separate fastest-compatible AFF3CT modes and report precision/schedule/batching differences, iteration distributions, and BER/FER counts and confidence intervals.\n\n- [hard] REQ-05: Satisfy the [Zen 3 measurement contract](dev/active/1a379447-zen3-cpu-performance/measurement-contract.md) for correctness, reproducible release benchmarks, comparison validity and adoption; receipts pin its committed version, the frozen protocol and the cell addendum. Include mandatory before/after evidence for production changes and preserve negative outcomes.\n\n## Notes\n\nKeep this issue profiling-only. Reuse the linked comparison harness; no AVX-512/GFNI or GPU kernel implementation is included. The evidence contains profile.md and machine-readable measurements under the issue's configured dev/bench_results directory, with durable links to the raw execution log and profiler artifacts.\n\n\n",
